Files in this directory derived from epdoptimize, and so covered by the
Apache License, Version 2.0:

    palette.go   colour-space maths and the calibrated display palettes,
                 from src/dither/processing.ts and
                 src/dither/data/default-palettes.json
    tone.go      the tone pipeline - paper normalisation, tone mapping,
                 LAB dynamic range compression, level compression -
                 from src/dither/processing.ts
    dither.go    the diffusion kernels and the palette matching modes,
                 from src/dither/data/diffusion-maps.ts and
                 src/dither/functions/find-closest-palette-color.ts
    preset.go    the processing presets, from src/dither/processing.ts

main.go and dither_test.go are original to this repository and are MIT
licensed, as is everything else outside this directory.

Changes made to the original work
---------------------------------

The ported files are not a verbatim copy. As required by section 4(b) of
the licence, the changes are:

  * Translated from TypeScript to Go, and from operating on a browser
    canvas ImageData to operating on a plain RGB byte slice with a stride
    of 3 rather than 4.

  * Error diffusion was rewritten around a three-row ring buffer instead
    of a full-image error buffer, so that source images of any size can be
    dithered without allocating hundreds of megabytes.

  * Added a "weighted" colour matching mode, which is this repository's own
    earlier brightness-weighted RGB distance and has no equivalent upstream.

  * Added a "none" preset, and renamed the palettes to the naming scheme
    used by this tool's -palette flag. Added a "pimoroni" palette, which is
    this repository's own pair of reference palettes, not upstream's.

  * Omitted, rather than ported: the "clarity" local-contrast stage, the
    "fast" dynamic-range-compression path, the WebAssembly kernels, the
    web worker scheduling, the ordered/random/blue-noise/Riemersma/
    simple2D/hueMix/coverage dithering modes, the image-style classifier
    and the automatic preset recommender.

  * The palette entries were reduced to the six inks of the EL133UF1 panel
    and reordered to that controller's colour-code order.
